  "anomaly_detected": false,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "Tracing the wires and labels across all three sheets, every interface matches the specification: the MCU supply/VSS pins, BOOT0 and NRST (with the 10k pull-up to VCC and the reset line shared with the Tag-Connect header), the NFC I2C bus with its three 10k pull-ups and VOUT tied to VCC, the SSD1306 I2C strapping (BS0=GND, BS1=VCC, BS2=GND; D0=SCL, D1/D2=SDA; CS#/D/C#/E/RD#/R/W#/D3-D7=GND) with its 10k pull-ups, the charge-pump network (1u/1u flying caps, 4.7u VCOMH, 2.2u VDD bypass, 390k IREF), the touch block (1k series resistor to the electrode, 22n sampling capacitor to GND, shield to GND), and the SWD header all correspond to the spec. The apparent differences are reference-designator renumbering (MCU U1, NFC U2, OLED U3, header J2, electrode A1, antenna A2) and auto-generated NET00xx labels, neither of which is an anomaly, and the antenna matching capacitor left as '??' is a documented open item in the spec, not a defect."
}

